<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Short Riders Rainy Weather</h1>
<p>Hanoi rain is usually brief, heavy, and predictable in season, and it changes the way a short rider should use a 50cc motorbike. A low seat and both feet planted firmly on the ground already give shorter riders an edge on wet streets, because balance corrections happen faster when your soles reach the pavement. Our shop at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien rents 50cc scooters for 200,000 VND per day and stays open from 09:00 to 21:00 every day, so you can collect a bike before the clouds build, or swap a soaked afternoon for a dry morning without pressure.</p>
<p>This page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a> and is written for riders of shorter stature. For rates across every model, see the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a>, and for rental terms in plain language, the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> collects the questions we hear most often at the counter.</p>
